  "description": "Route C step 2 (bean qou-8uxw): the framework's q-deformation of the Burnside fixed-point count is the PIVOTAL (K-weighted) trace, not the unweighted count. On V^{⊗4} the ordinary trace (Dipper–James / BHW count-shaped reading, z_J = (3q − q⁻¹)/4) and the convention-D pivotal trace (z_D = q³/(q²+1)) agree at q = 1 and to first order, and differ exactly by z_J − z_D = −(q²−1)²/(4q(q²+1)). The ordinary trace is NOT a Markov trace: the partial trace of R over the last strand is diag(2q − q⁻¹, q), scalar iff q² = 1, and the Markov property fails on S₃; the pivotal weight makes it scalar. Both traces are integer Laurent polynomials on all 24 words of S₄, so integrality does not separate them — the Markov property does. Consequence: an unweighted groupoid cardinality cannot be the framework's q-count; a BHW reading needs a WEIGHTED cardinality (weight q^{#0 − #1} per colouring), which the held BHW paper does not supply. Scope (a): n = 4, spin-½, convention D. Nothing fitted or wired.",
