    "verdict": "NEGATIVE for the unweighted reading, with the invariant named: a trace on V^{⊗n} is a Markov trace (hence a closure invariant) iff the partial trace of R over the closed strand is scalar; for the unweighted count it is diag(2q − q⁻¹, q), scalar iff q² = 1. So the q-deformation of the fixed-point count that the framework uses is the K-weighted count — route C's step 2 needs a weighted groupoid cardinality, not BHW's unweighted one. The two readings share value and slope at q = 1 and split at second order. REFINED (5b): the K-weight is itself a cardinality — q^{l(w)} [2]^n tr_D(w) = Σ_k q^{n−2k} N_k(w) with N_k(w) ∈ Z[Q] non-negative at every prime power Q = q² tested; taking the framework's q itself as the prime power p (5c), the counts live over F_{p²} and the weights p^{n−2k} over the index-2 subfield F_p as |F_p^{n−2k}| or |B(F_p^{2k−n})|, so the convention-D trace IS a groupoid cardinality of ⊔_k Fix_k(w) × A_k for EVERY n (measured at n = 3, 4). What fails is only the unweighted reading."
